prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a migratory bird migration path visualization. 6 storks fly along a curved path.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/Fox.glb;
(2) Clone 6 instances and distribute them along the path with front-to-back spacing;
(3) Play the flying animation on each instance;

[Migration Path]
(4) Use CatmullRomCurve3 to define a curved path spanning the scene;
(5) Path control points: (0,10,0), (20,12,20), (40,8,40), (60,15,20), (80,10,0), (100,12,-20);
(6) Visualize the path using TubeGeometry or Line;

[Path Following]
(7) The birds move along the path and face in the direction of the path tangent;
(8) The 6 birds have slightly different speeds (base speed 5 m/s ± random 20%);

[Time Control]
(9) Time multiplier slider (id="timeScale", range 0.5-5, default 1);

[Camera Tracking]
(10) Click any bird (Raycaster) to switch the camera to follow that bird;
(11) Click an empty area again to restore the free view (OrbitControls);

[Terrain]
(12) A simple ground plane with a green texture or color;

[HUD Display]
(13) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Distance traveled (id="distance", path progress percentage of the frontmost bird)
  - Group spread (id="spread", distance between the frontmost and rearmost birds)
  - Time multiplier (id="timeValue")
  - Tracked bird number (id="trackedBird", -1 means none)

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean
  - birdCount: number (6)
  - leadDistance: number (lead bird's path progress, 0-1)
  - spread: number
  - timeScale: number
  - trackedBird: number (-1 or 0-5)

Output a standalone HTML file.
